message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "NeuroSim 3D: Interactive Brain & Neuron Firing Simulator"
abstract: >-
  An interactive browser simulation of spiking neurons inside a 3D human brain.
  Thousands of leaky integrate-and-fire neurons are placed in seven anatomical
  regions and wired by nearest-neighbour and long-range synapses with
  distance-dependent delays and excitatory or inhibitory weights. Users can
  stimulate regions or single points, switch between mental-state presets
  (rest, focus, deep sleep, caffeine, seizure, anaesthesia), tune neuron
  dynamics and watch spikes, signal pulses and an EEG-like activity trace in
  real time. English and Turkish interfaces.
